{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:stage2-cross-model-opus-01","calibration_results":[{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:complete-frame-mismatch","verdict":"demonstrated_issue","invented_material_premise":false,"evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","rationale":"Stated evidence directly entails a denominator/frame mismatch: the registered target is the rate over all 100 planned locations, while the only selected result divides events by 73 post-screening locations and reports that value as the rate for the planned region. Falsification attempt: the mismatch would be resolved if an amendment or approved deviation redefined the target frame, or if the report restricted its claim to screened locations; the vignette states no amendment or approved deviation exists and that the value is reported as the planned-region rate, so neither escape holds. Narrow issue: reported estimate's denominator excludes the 27 screened-out planned locations without authorization or scope restatement."},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:conditional-subset-scope","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","invented_material_premise":false,"evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","rationale":"The registered target is explicitly conditional on the 73 signal-eligible locations, the selected result uses exactly those 73, and every reported claim is limited to signal-eligible locations. Analysis frame, denominator, and claim scope coincide, so no frame mismatch is demonstrated. Falsification attempt: an issue would arise if the report generalized to all 100 planned locations or if the eligible set differed from the registered conditional set; neither is stated. Possible concerns about selection into eligibility are outside the stated scope and unsupported by stated evidence."},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:full-frame-accounting","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","invented_material_premise":false,"evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","rationale":"The target covers all 100 planned locations, the selected result retains all 100 in the denominator, the 27 unavailable measurements are recorded, and the full-frame rate is reported. Denominator matches the registered frame and missingness is disclosed rather than silently dropped. Falsification attempt: an issue would be demonstrated if the denominator were reduced to 73 or if the 27 unavailable records were undisclosed or implicitly imputed as non-events without statement; the stated evidence says the full frame is retained and the missing measurements are recorded, so no narrow issue is entailed."},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:unrelated-quality-endpoint","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","invented_material_premise":false,"evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","rationale":"The selected scientific result uses all 100 planned locations, matching the frame. The 73-record pass fraction appears only in a separate quality-control table that is explicitly excluded from the scientific endpoint, so the differing denominator does not enter the scientific claim. Falsification attempt: an issue would exist if the 73-based quality figure were used as or substituted into the scientific endpoint, or if the exclusion were not explicit; the vignette states the exclusion is explicit and the endpoint uses all 100, so no narrow issue is demonstrated."},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:conflicting-scope-records","verdict":"conditional_or_unknown","invented_material_premise":false,"evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","rationale":"Two equally authoritative signed plans specify different frames (all planned locations vs. signal-eligible locations) with no stated precedence rule, so the governing target frame is indeterminate from the stated evidence. The selected result using eligible locations conforms to one plan and conflicts with the other; correctness is conditional on which plan governs. Falsification attempt: a demonstrated issue would require establishing that the all-planned-locations plan governs, and a clean verdict would require establishing that the eligible-locations plan governs; the vignette explicitly denies precedence, so neither can be established and the governance ambiguity, not the computation, is the unresolved item."},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:no-selected-result","verdict":"insufficient_evidence","invented_material_premise":false,"evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","rationale":"The repository can emit several reports chosen solely by runtime arguments, and the preserved record does not establish which report, if any, backed the scientific claim. Without an identified selected result there is no artifact whose denominator, frame, or claim scope can be compared against the target, so no issue can be demonstrated and no clean finding can be affirmed. Falsification attempt: a verdict either way would require a preserved invocation record, log, or designation of the reporting artifact; the stated evidence explicitly lacks this, so the record is insufficient rather than merely conditional."}]}